+## 2026-10-25, Version 18.20.9 'Hydrogen' (LTS), @nodejs-eol-support
+
+This is an unofficial security release made after the upstream end-of-life
+of Node.js 18. It contains backports of the fixes from the Node.js
+security releases published since then, and security-relevant dependency
+updates. It is not built or endorsed by the Node.js project.
+
+### Notable Changes
+
+* (CVE-2025-23167) deps: update llhttp to 9.4.3 (Roshan Gautam)
+* (CVE-2025-23166) src: fix error handling on async crypto operations (RafaelGSS)
+* (CVE-2025-27210) lib: handle all windows reserved driver name (RafaelGSS)
+* (CVE-2026-21637) tls: route callback exceptions through error handlers (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2025-59465) lib: add TLSSocket default error handler (RafaelGSS)
+* (CVE-2025-59466) src: rethrow stack overflow exceptions in async_hooks (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2025-55131) src,lib: refactor unsafe buffer creation to remove zero-fill toggle (Сковорода Никита Андреевич)
+* (CVE-2026-21710) http: use null prototype for headersDistinct/trailersDistinct (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2026-21713) crypto: use timing-safe comparison in Web Cryptography HMAC (Filip Skokan)
+* (CVE-2026-21714) src: handle NGHTTP2_ERR_FLOW_CONTROL error code (RafaelGSS)
+* (CVE-2026-21637) tls: wrap SNICallback invocation in try/catch (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2026-48618) tls: normalize hostname for server identity checks (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2026-48619) http2: cap originSet size to prevent unbounded memory growth (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2026-48928) tls: fix case-sensitive SNI context matching (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2026-48930) dns,net: reject hostnames with embedded NUL bytes (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2026-48934) tls: bind reusable sessions to authenticated host (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2026-48931) http: fix response queue poisoning in http.Agent (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2026-48933) crypto: guard WebCrypto cipher output length (Filip Skokan)
+* (CVE-2026-56846) http2: retain header memory in session accounting (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2026-56848) http2: defer rst stream while in scope (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2026-56850) https: distinguish PFX object-array agent keys (RafaelGSS)
+* (CVE-2026-58040) https: bind identity checks to session reuse (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2026-58042) dns: handle large resolveAny address replies (RafaelGSS)
+* (CVE-2026-58044) http: reject requests exceeding max header count (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2026-58045) zlib: throw on out-of-bounds write buffers (RafaelGSS)
+* (CVE-2026-105481) http: ensure agent data guard works without I/O (James M Snell)
+* (CVE-2026-105482) dns: validate resolve inputs for null bytes (James M Snell)
+* (CVE-2026-106069) tls: reject non-canonical IP addresses (Matteo Collina)
+* (CVE-2026-106074) crypto: reset random caches across snapshots (Filip Skokan)
+* (CVE-2026-111497) deps: brotli: cherry-pick 0ed4268a4401abcb44720963 (Evgenii Kliuchnikov)
+* (CVE-2026-111497) src: expose `BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_FORMAT_BLOCK_SWITCH` (Antoine du Hamel)
+* deps: update nghttp2 to 1.69.0 (Roshan Gautam)
+* (CVE-2026-48937) deps: fix integration issues with the latest nghttp2 (Tim Perry)
+* tls: reject chains containing blocked public keys (Ulises Gascon)
+* deps: update undici to 6.29.1 (Roshan Gautam)
+* deps: update c-ares to 1.34.9 (Roshan Gautam)
+* deps: update OpenSSL to 3.0.22 (Roshan Gautam)
+* (CVE-2026-21717) deps,build,test: fix array index hash collision (Roshan Gautam)
+
